     The uussffss driver provides support for emulating an USB mass storage device
     when the USB stack is activated in USB device side mode (the
     usb_template(4) module is loaded and the _h_w_._u_s_b_._t_e_m_p_l_a_t_e sysctl is set to
     0).

     Upon attach the driver creates a RAM disk which can be read and written.

